所以，还有蒂姆说：“我真的觉得这是一个好人。”

00:58:03.045 --> 00:58:06.097
And I'm supposed, we're supposed to be in each other's lives.
“而且我觉得，我们注定要出现在彼此的生命里。”

00:58:06.097 --> 00:58:07.849
And she's feeling like a lost soul.
而她觉得自己像个迷失的灵魂。

00:58:07.849 --> 00:58:09.600
I want to bring her into our group.
“我想把她带进我们的圈子里。”

00:58:09.600 --> 00:58:13.002
She does, she said she hasn't met many good people here in New York.
她确实说过，她在纽约没遇到几个好人。

00:58:13.002 --> 00:58:13.502
Right.
没错。

00:58:13.502 --> 00:58:15.404
I really like the fact that she's new.
我很喜欢她是新来的人这一点。

00:58:15.404 --> 00:58:15.904
Yeah.
对。

00:58:15.904 --> 00:58:17.255
She's new to New York City.
她刚来到纽约市。

00:58:17.255 --> 00:58:20.157
You know, I really like I really felt that in that moment.
你知道，我真的很喜欢，那一刻我真的感同身受。

00:58:20.157 --> 00:58:21.558
She played that beautifully.
她把那种情绪演得很绝。

00:58:21.558 --> 00:58:22.709
It was very vulnerable.
非常脆弱。

00:58:22.260 --> 00:58:23.600
I haven't met many good people.
“我没遇到几个好人。”

00:58:23.600 --> 00:58:28.272
You remember that moment when you first moved to New York in your 20s and you're like, it's such a big city.
你还记得你二十多岁刚搬到纽约时的情景吗？你会觉得，这是一座多么巨大的城市啊。

00:58:28.272 --> 00:58:29.699
How am I going to make my people?
我该怎么找到属于我的圈子呢？

00:58:31.139 --> 00:58:35.219
I kind of had it baked in just because I went right into grad school and I had this community.
我当时其实是顺理成章地融入进去了，因为我直接读了研究生，然后就有了这个社群。

00:58:35.219 --> 00:58:36.350
But I remember in L.A.
但我记得在洛杉矶，

00:58:36.350 --> 00:58:40.099
it took me a while to, you know, it takes you a while to find your tribe.
我花了点时间，你知道的，你得花时间去寻找你的同类。

00:58:40.099 --> 00:58:44.910
And big cities especially are incredibly disorienting before you find your neighborhood.
大城市尤其如此，在找到你熟悉的街区之前，会让人感到极其迷茫。

00:58:44.910 --> 00:58:48.300
You love of the community you love, and you have to have that.
你所热爱的社群，你必须得拥有这些。

00:58:48.300 --> 00:58:52.659
I mean, you can't, big cities are so isolating and could be so overwhelming.
我是说，你不能……大城市太孤立了，也太容易让人不知所措了。

00:58:53.860 --> 00:59:10.940
But yeah, I thought, I was really taken with that and I think Jordan and I was also pointing to what we were talking about earlier that, I always think of it like life, like surviving a reptite or undertow.
不过，是的，我觉得，我真的很喜欢这一点，而且我觉得乔丹和我也是在呼应我们之前讨论过的话题，我总是把它比作生活，就像在离岸流或暗流中挣扎求生一样。

00:59:10.940 --> 00:59:14.579
Like if you fight the undertow, it takes you down.
如果你跟暗流抗争，它就会把你拽下去。

00:59:14.579 --> 00:59:19.139
It's really dangerous, but if you let it take you, it pops you back up.
这真的很危险，但如果你顺从它，它就会把你托回水面。

00:59:19.139 --> 00:59:19.980
Yeah.
对。

00:59:19.980 --> 00:59:29.139
And it feels like in these first two episode Ted, he tries to fight and tries to fight and he's drowning until he just lets it take him.
感觉在前两集里，特德一直在抗争，一直在挣扎，他觉得自己快要溺水了，直到他选择顺其自然。

00:59:29.139 --> 00:59:35.559
You know, and he pops up and he's doing okay.
你知道的，然后他浮了上来，一切都挺好的。

